cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use COMPASS in research or teaching, please cite the software
  using the information provided in this file. If you modify or
  redistribute COMPASS, retain the required origin and copyright notices.
type: software
title: "COMPASS – A planning and assessment tool for archaeological object documentation"
version: "1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Weßling"
    given-names: "Ronny"
abstract: >-
  COMPASS is a web-based planning and assessment tool for archaeological
  object documentation. It supports the definition of intended uses,
  documentation requirements, documentation forms, and quality target
  profiles, and allows prospective planning or retrospective assessment
  by comparing target requirements with practice or existing-data profiles.
  The application provides rule-based guidance and documents decisions,
  limitations, and resulting conclusions.
keywords:
  - archaeology
  - archaeological documentation
  - cultural heritage
  - 3D digitisation
  - decision support
  - quality assessment
  - research software
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/RonnyWessling/COMPASS-A-planning-and-assessment-tool-for-archaeological-object-documentation"
url: "https://ronnywessling.github.io/COMPASS-A-planning-and-assessment-tool-for-archaeological-object-documentation/"
